The original problem was that schemas built using `z.record()` were not getting recognised because the JSONSchema7 representation for this zod schema is:
```
{
  type: 'object',
  properties: {},
  additionalProperties: {} // what's inside depends on how z.record was called. For example:
   // when using z.record(z.string(), z.string()), the additionalProperties will be { type: "string" }
}
```

See that properties is an empty object? That is why the entire schema was not considered a candidate for conversion and returned as `undefined`. The fix for this is the method `isEmptyObjectSchema`, [these lines](https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/6919/files#diff-db99b750a11626b268f6fea2df8c2f94414eaf3adbe3cfa358832b7f18d574a4R135-R136) particularly. Its only the rest of the changes in method `convertJSONSchemaToOpenAPISchema` that we are reverting.

